Hey [~accountid:613f557334599600711bb8d5] can you please forward the following response to the Courier?



{quote}Dear *Aleksander*,

Thank you for your request, which was received by us on *21 November 2025*. 

In your request you asked us to explain why your contact details were visible to the Client during an active delivery.

Below is our explanation.

Your contact details were shown to the Client during an active delivery to comply with the Digital Services Act (*“DSA”*). Under Article 30(1) of the DSA, providers of online platforms that allow consumers to conclude distance contracts with traders, such as Bolt, must make certain trader information available on the online platform. This includes, among other things, the trader’s name and contact details, which must be visible at least on the online interface where information on the product or service is presented to the consumer. We would like to point out that Delivery Partners are considered traders for the purpose of the Article 30(1) of the DSA.



For information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Notice at[ |https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/][https://bolt.eu/et-ee/privacy/privacy-for-couriers/?category=delivery|https://bolt.eu/et-ee/privacy/privacy-for-couriers/?category=delivery|smart-link] , which includes further information about:

* The categories of personal data we process;
* The purposes for which we process personal data;
* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;
* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;
* The sources of personal data received from other parties;
* Your rights in relation to your personal data;
* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making/profiling of personal data; and
* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.

*Your rights*

In addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify, erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data or to object to such processing. Any such requests that are received will be considered in conjunction with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws.

If you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection or supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.

If you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this email.

Yours sincerely,

Bolt{quote}



Next time, when there is a privacy-related request (concerning personal data) you can escalate the case internally via Beehive to CS Privacy Compliance Tier. 🙂  They’ll pick it up and raise it with us.

